364 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The primary purpose of this project is to design and develop a functional prototype that leverages machine learning to assist medical practitioners in the diagnosis and prognosis of kidney tumors. The system is built to deliver on three core capabilities:)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
365 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (1. Tumor Classification: To accurately classify kidney tumors from medical images \(e.g., CT scans or MRIs\) into relevant categories, such as benign or malignant, providing a crucial data point for initial diagnosis.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
366 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (2. Growth Prediction: To provide a predictive analysis of the tumor's potential growth rate over a specified period. This feature aims to help clinicians assess the urgency and type of intervention required.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
367 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (3. Accessible Interface: To present these complex analyses through a clear, intuitive, and interactive JavaScript-based web interface, making the technology accessible to clinicians without requiring specialized technical expertise.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
