395 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (To ensure the successful development of a robust and reliable system, a structured, multi-stage methodology was employed. Each stage was clearly defined to guide the project from conception to completion.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
396 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (1. System Planning: This initial phase involved identifying the core functionalities and designing the overall system architecture. This included defining the client-server interaction model and creating the database schema for storing image metadata, user information, and prediction results)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
397 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
398 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (2. Data Acquisition & Preprocessing: A suitable dataset of anonymized medical kidney scans was gathered. This data underwent rigorous preprocessing, including normalization, resizing, and augmentation, to prepare it for effective model training and to prevent model overfitting.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
399 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (3. Backend Model Development: The machine learning models for tumor classification \(CNN\) and growth prediction \(regression model\) were built, trained, and validated in Python using frameworks like TensorFlow and Keras. Performance was meticulously evaluated using standard metrics to ensure accuracy and reliability.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
400 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (4. Frontend Development: The user interface was created using JavaScript and a modern web framework. The focus was on building an intuitive and responsive workflow for users to upload medical images, initiate the analysis, and clearly visualize the resulting predictions and growth projections.)
/Pg 16 0 R
