849 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The " Kidney Tumor Prediction and Growth Analysis" system successfully met its core objectives, culminating in a functional prototype that demonstrates the power of integrating artificial intelligence with modern web technologies for clinical decision support. The project achieved its key technical goals: a Convolutional Neural Network was developed and trained to classify kidney tumors with high accuracy, and this predictive engine was seamlessly integrated with an intuitive JavaScript frontend via a robust REST API. The resulting system provides a clear and efficient workflow for clinicians to upload medical scans and receive data-driven insights on tumor type and potential growth.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
850 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (As an educational endeavor and a proof-of-concept, this project holds significant value. It serves as a practical application of deep learning in the critical domain of medical imaging and establishes a scalable architectural foundation for future development. While the prototype is successful, its limitations are acknowledged, primarily concerning the size and diversity of the training dataset and the current scope of predictive features. Future work should focus on training the models on larger, multi-institutional datasets to improve generalization, incorporating additional predictive features \(such as patient demographics or biomarkers\), and ultimately, conducting rigorous clinical validation studies to assess its real-world efficacy. In conclusion, this project strongly affirms the transformative potential of AI to augment the capabilities of medical professionals, paving the way for more precise, personalized, and proactive healthcare diagnostics.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
